      "writtenOn": "2021-01-29T22:07:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What happens if a limited operation is set, but the port is not suspended?\n\nYou could add a check of !TC_FLAGS_SUSPEND \u0026\u0026 TC_FLAGS_USB_RETIMER_FW_UPDATE_LTD_RUN and set an error on last_mux_result.    Any result that sets both USB4 and TBT_COMPAT is not a valid mux setting - so you could define 0xFE as an error result.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3596,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3597,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "3db914bc541d6bf651f57f5d81fa8eb717e12e56",
