        "patchSetId": 35
      },
      "lineNbr": 3597,
      "author": {
        "id": 1116125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-02T00:36:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"#define USB_RETIMER_FW_UPDATE_ERR 0xfe\" is added in ec_commands.h to notify AP this condition check failure. In usb_retimer_fw_update.c, will check if PD is suspended by calling \"pd_is_port_enabled(port)\", if returns false, then set flag  TC_FLAGS_USB_RETIMER_FW_UPDATE_LTD_RUN so inside tc_run set mux USB/Safe/TBT/None can be called.\nTC_FLAGS_xxx and TC_xxx_FLAG() macros are defined in usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c, so can\u0027t access from outside, I have to add access functions to set UPDATE_RUN/UPDATE_LTD_RUN flags.",
